  "full_response": "Below is a sample Terraform variables file, typically named `variables.tf`, that defines the necessary variables to store the Azure configuration details. In addition, there's a corresponding `terraform.tfvars` file, usually for assigning actual values to those variables for use in your Terraform configurations.\n\n### `variables.tf`\n\n```hcl\nvariable \"azure_subscription_id\" {\n  description = \"The Azure Subscription ID.\"\n  type        = string\n}\n\nvariable \"azure_client_secret\" {\n  description = \"The Client Secret for Azure App Registration.\"\n  type        = string\n}\n\nvariable \"azure_tenant_id\" {\n  description = \"The Azure Tenant ID.\"\n  type        = string\n}\n\nvariable \"azure_storage_account_access_key\" {\n  description = \"The Access Key for an Azure Storage Account.\"\n  type        = string\n}\n```\n\n### `terraform.tfvars`\n\n```hcl\n# terraform.tfvars\n# Make sure to store this file securely and avoid committing it to version control if it contains sensitive information.\n\nazure_subscription_id   = \"your-azure-subscription-id\"\nazure_client_secret     = \"your-azure-client-secret\"\nazure_tenant_id         = \"your-azure-tenant-id\"\nazure_storage_account_access_key = \"your-azure-storage-account-access-key\"\n```\n\n### Security Considerations\n\n- **Sensitive Data:** Be cautious with handling sensitive information such as your client secret and storage account access key. Avoid committing your `terraform.tfvars` file to source control if it contains sensitive information. Instead, leverage environment variables or a secure vaulting solution (like Azure Key Vault) for such data.\n  \n- **Access Management:** Assign the minimum necessary permissions to the Azure service principal used by Terraform to interact with your Azure resources.\n\n- **Environment Variables:** You can also use environment variables to set these values. Terraform can automatically use variables with the prefix `TF_VAR_`. For example:\n  ```shell\n  export TF_VAR_azure_subscription_id=your-azure-subscription-id\n  export TF_VAR_azure_client_secret=your-azure-client-secret\n  export TF_VAR_azure_tenant_id=your-azure-tenant-id\n  export TF_VAR_azure_storage_account_access_key=your-azure-storage-account-access-key\n  ```\n\nBy following these guidelines, you'll ensure a more secure and maintainable setup for managing your Azure infrastructure with Terraform.",
